## DESCRIPTION
## Linear Algebra
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by cmd6a 5/3/06

## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Matrices)
## DBsection(Matrix algebra)
## Date(July 2013)
## Institution(Rochester and Hope College)
## Author(Paul Pearson)
## Level(4)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('Linear Algebra with Applications')
## AuthorText1('Jeffrey Holt')
## EditionText1('1')
## Section1('3.2')
## Problem1('')
## KEYWORDS('linear algebra','matrix','linear system')

######################################
#  Initialization

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

#######################################
#  Setup

Context('Matrix')->variables->are(x => 'Real', y => 'Real');

$a = non_zero_random(-9, 9, 1);
$b = non_zero_random(-9, 9, 1);

$x    = 1 - $b;
$ynum = $b * $x;
$y    = Compute("$ynum/$a");
$ab   = $a * $b;
$b2   = $b**2;

$A = Matrix([ [ 'x', $a ], [ 'y', $b ], ]);

$As11 = Formula("x^2+$a*y")->reduce();
$As12 = Formula("$a*x+$ab")->reduce();
$As21 = Formula("x*y+$b*y")->reduce();
$As22 = Formula("$a*y+$b2")->reduce();

$As = Matrix([ [ $As11, $As12 ], [ $As21, $As22 ] ]);

#######################################
#  Main text

BEGIN_PGML
If [` A = [$A]`], determine the values of [`x`] and [`y`] for which [`A^2=A`].

* [`x=`][_]{$x}{5}
* [`y=`][_]{$y}{5}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
[`A^2=[$A][$A]=[$As]`].

Now set [`A^2=A`]:
[```[$As]=[$A]```]
Comparing the 1,2-entries gives [`[$As12]=[$a]`], so [`x=[$x]`].

Comparing the 2,2-entries gives [`[$As22]=[$b]`], so [`y=[$y->{correct_ans_latex_string}]`].

You can verify that these values of [`x`] and [`y`] cause the other entries to be equal.
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
